// ===================== 13.5 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('13.5  The figure you cannot remember'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The figure\'s name and not the figure**, which is the instruction the room will break first. **Everybody has one and about half have three.** **The board matters here for one reason only: it is the evidence that this is the ordinary condition of anybody who writes with numbers in it** — **and a student who thinks they are the only one who cannot produce a figure from their own document will guess in the room rather than say so.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Usable: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **Both carry the three things.** **2 gives the register, Thursday and a range; 4 gives the regional office, this morning and an order of magnitude.** **1 and 5 hand the question back** — _I cannot remember_, _I would rather not guess_ — **and 3 is the one that costs most**: _about twenty per cent, I think_ is a number with a hedge on it, **and a panel will quote the number and drop the hedge.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **three things**: where the figure is, when you can produce it, and the order of magnitude you do remember.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** **The second-year uptake, from her own interim report.** ⚠ **Her three things: the register, Thursday, and between a fifth and a quarter.**   **2** ⚠ **It is a number with a hedge on it, and a reader quotes the number and drops the hedge** — **and then she is the candidate who said twenty when the register says thirty-one.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The distinction between a range and a hedged number is the technical content of this cycle and it is worth ten minutes on its own, because the room has it backwards.** **_A fifth to a quarter_ excludes a half and excludes a twentieth: it is a precise statement about a wide interval.** **_About twenty, I think_ is an imprecise statement about a narrow one** — **which is the worst of the available answers and the one everybody gives first.** **Put both on the board and ask which can be quoted against the speaker.** ⚠ **Only the second can, because the range is the claim and a hedge is detachable.** **This is 4.5 and 9.1 arriving together, in speech, under pressure** — **and it is the first time in the course that a student has had to produce either without a page in front of them.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A figure in a register** — _it is in the register; I can have it to you by Thursday; and what I remember is that it was between a fifth and a quarter._   **2** **One held by another office** — _the regional office holds it, I have asked this morning, and the order of magnitude is hundreds and not thousands._   **3** ⚠ **One whose location you do not know** — **that is the first thing and it is said plainly**: _I do not know which register holds it; the regional office will, and I shall ask today._   **4** **One you are carrying** — ⚠ **produce it.** **The move does not apply.**   **5** **One where the order of magnitude answers the real question** — **and you will usually not know that it does until afterwards.**'));
