out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Rizk was asked in October for the uptake figure for the second year, which is in her own interim report, and she could not produce it. Mr Shihabi said and you said so, and she said I cannot remember and then waited, which is three words and leaves the panel holding the question. Mrs Khoury said a panel then does the only thing it can: it asks for the figure anyway, or it asks somebody else, or it writes the answer down as not known to the candidate, and all three are worse than the answer that was available. Mrs Oueidat said three things, and none of them is the figure, and Mrs Rizk gave them: where it is, when she can produce it, and what she does remember, which is that it was between a fifth and a quarter, twenty-six words, and the panel moved on. Dr Qabbani said a fifth to a quarter is a guess, and Mrs Oueidat said it is a range and the difference is not a nicety: about twenty per cent, I think, is a number with a hedge on it and a panel will quote the number and drop the hedge, and then you are the candidate who said twenty when the register says thirty-one. Mrs Tarabishi said so the vaguer answer is the safer one, and Mrs Khoury said it is not vaguer at all: a fifth to a quarter excludes a half and excludes a twentieth, so it is a precise statement about a wide interval, where about twenty, I think, is an imprecise statement about a narrow one. Mr Tayara asked about the date, and it has to be specific and it has to be a day she will keep, because as soon as possible is not a commitment and a panel knows it. Mrs Ajouz asked what happens if you do not know where it is either, and then that is the first thing and it is said plainly, because not knowing where a figure is kept is a fact about a system. Mr Zahreddine said his was a calibration date and he had it in his pocket, and then he produces it and the cycle does not apply. Mr Attar asked whether the order of magnitude ever helps, and Mrs Rizk said it is the half the panel used: they were deciding whether the second year had been worth funding, and a fifth to a quarter answered that and thirty-one per cent would not have answered it better. And Mrs Rizk said the thing she will take away is the three words: I cannot remember is true and honest and hands the question back, and the twenty-six words were available and nobody had ever shown her there was anything else to say.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to carry out of the cycle: the twenty-six words were available and nobody had ever shown her there was anything else to say.** **_I cannot remember_ is true and honest and hands the question back.** **The room will defend it as honesty** — **and the answer is that the three-part version is also honest and does the reader\'s work as well, which is the whole difference between truthfulness and usefulness.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ _About twenty per cent, I think._ → **a number with a detachable hedge; the number will be quoted.**   **2** _As soon as possible._ → **not a commitment, and a reader knows it.**   **3** ⚠ **A range that excludes nothing** → **a refusal with numbers on it.**   **4** **The three-part answer about a figure in the candidate\'s own hand** → **evasion about a document they are holding.**   **5** ⚠ **The location omitted when it is not known** → **one gap turned into two.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Thirty-one per cent: two hundred and six of six hundred and sixty-four, for the twelve months to 30 June.** **It is above the range she gave on Tuesday by six percentage points**, and she reports that plainly because a range given under questioning is a claim.'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **She was remembering the first year, which was twenty-two per cent and which she has quoted in four documents.** **The shape is displacement and not absence** — **a figure she could not retrieve had been pushed out by one she knew well, which is why the remedy is a card with three figures and not an instruction to remember harder.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **Three figures on one card: first-year and second-year uptake, each with its denominator and period, and the date of the register page.** **Not more than three, because a candidate carrying eleven figures retrieves none of them** — **and she had eleven in a folder on Tuesday and produced none.**'));
