// ===================== 13.6 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('13.6  The note they read before you arrive'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The reader and the document, and the second question is the one that matters: have you seen it?** **Nine of ten have such a reader and only three have seen the document, and the three who have seen it did not write it.** **That is the position the cycle is designed around** — **and a student who has never seen what is written about them before they walk in is the normal case and should be told so.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Belong: **1** and **3**. ⚠ **Both are countable or scoped.** **1 has two numbers and its limit inside it; 3 is a scope sentence with the exclusion named.** **2, 4 and 5 all fail the same test**: could this be read aloud against me? **_I have worked hard_, _a significant contribution_, _I am confident_** — **and the room should be made to say what has no defence in each, which is that none of the three has any content to defend.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **choosing which of your sentences they will quote**, because they will quote one and three hundred words decides which.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **One question: could this be read aloud against me?** **Every sentence has to survive it, and _significant_ has no defence because it has no content.**   **2** **The denominator sentence** — _nine findings at four degrees of certainty, each degree stated in the sentence that carries the finding_ — ⚠ **and the chair read it out and asked her to take the four degrees in turn, which is the forty minutes she had prepared and the only forty minutes she had prepared.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the cycle that explains the whole unit, so it is worth saying what it does to the other six.** **The note decides the questions.** **13.1 to 13.5 are moves for answering, and 13.6 is the move that chooses what will be asked** — **and a class that has done the five answering cycles and not this one has learnt to defend a document whose questions somebody else selected.** **Mrs Tarabishi\'s forty minutes is the evidence**: she prepared one thing and it was the one thing asked, because she had made it the most countable sentence on the page. ⚠ **The mechanism is not persuasion and must not be taught as persuasion.** **A panel reading three hundred words of prose opens where something can be counted**, and the writer controls where that is. **Say the mechanism plainly and the room will stop trying to write a note that flatters.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **With two numbers in it** — _nine findings at four degrees of certainty._   **2** **With its limit inside it** — _each degree stated in the sentence that carries the finding._   **3** **A scope sentence** — _two bays behind sheeted scaffold were not inspected and the finding excludes them._   **4** ⚠ **One you would cut, and why** — _I believe the work represents a significant contribution_: **no content, so no defence.**   **5** ⚠ **One that could be read aloud against you** — **and the test is not whether it is false but whether it can be argued with on a word you chose carelessly.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
