out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **That the minute is wrong.** **It is not wrong and that is why.** **Every word of it is true: he was unable to say the figure, and the panel noted that the submission rests on it** — **and the second half is the only part that is a judgement, and it is the only part that can be answered.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the first mediation of Book 2 and the thirteenth of the level, and one thing about it is new: the other party has acted and the record exists.** **In Book 1 every mediation was between parties who could still change their minds.** **Here there is a minute, and a minute is a fact.** **So the method narrows: separate the record into facts and judgements, leave every fact alone, and answer the one judgement.** _He was unable to say the figure_ **is a fact.** _The submission rests on it_ **is a judgement.** ⚠ **Put both sentences on the board and make the room sort them before anything is drafted** — **and expect the room to want to answer the first, because the first is the one that stings.** **It is also the one that is true.**'));
