out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Khoury said the chair gets the letter and nobody else is a candidate, because the panel has acted, the minute is the record, and Mr Tayara is the only party who can say what the figure was for. Mr Tayara said what must not be said is that the minute is wrong, and it is not wrong and that is why: every word of it is true, and the only part that is a judgement is that the submission rests on the figure, which is the part to answer. Mrs Oueidat said so the letter answers one sentence, and Mrs Tarabishi gave it: the submission does not rest on that figure, six words, and then the arithmetic, four hundred and ten pupils, two rooms, annexe A, all three of which were in the note three weeks before the panel sat. Dr Qabbani asked why they remembered the other sentence, and Mrs Khoury said because it is the only sentence in the note with I have not been able to in it: he wrote a limitation, correctly, as 13.6 requires, and the limitation was the most quotable thing on the page because nothing else in the note was countable in the way a limitation is. Mr Shihabi said so the limitation was a mistake, and Mrs Oueidat said the limitation was right and its position was wrong, which is 13.3: a limitation with no competing countable sentence near it becomes the sentence. Mrs Rizk asked what would have prevented it, and one sentence that was available: four hundred and ten pupils and two afternoon rooms, the arithmetic is at annexe A and needs no governorate figure, twenty-one words and two numbers. Mrs Khoury said and one more sentence, which is the uncomfortable one, that the note did not say what the governorate figure was for, because a letter that corrects a minute without conceding anything reads as a complaint. Mr Zahreddine asked whether the chair does not come out of it badly, and the chair comes out of it as the only person who told him what happened, and nobody had to say that. Mrs Ajouz asked what you ask for, and one thing, and it is not that the minute be changed, because a record altered afterwards is worth less to everybody including him. Mr Attar said so the minute stands, and the minute stands and the submission is reconsidered, and those are two different requests: eight of ten first drafts asked for the first. And Mr Tayara said the thing he will take away is the three weeks: they read it on the fourth and sat on the twenty-first, and what survived seventeen days was the one sentence he was most careful about, and he had thought carefulness was the protection.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to carry out of the unit: they read it on the fourth and sat on the twenty-first, and what survived seventeen days was the one sentence he was most careful about, and he had thought carefulness was the protection.** **It is the sentence that makes 13.6 necessary rather than merely useful** — **carefulness chooses the words and position chooses the question, and only one of the two is under the writer\'s control after the document has gone.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ _The minute is inaccurate._ → **it is accurate, and this is the one answerable sentence in the letter.**   **2** **A request that the minute be amended** → **that is asking the panel to say it was careless.**   **3** ⚠ **No concession** → **a correction with no cost reads as a grievance.**   **4** **A concession that is large** → **it hands the panel a second finding; the cost has to be real and small.**   **5** ⚠ **A sentence blaming the chair for remembering the wrong line** → **the chair is the only party who said what happened, and nobody had to.**   **6** **A letter written on Pair B** → **there is no judgement in that record.**'));
