out.push(A('**1** **which**   **2** **but**   **3** **on**   **4** **sooner**   **5** **were**   **6** **be**   **7** **than**   **8** **far**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 2 is grammar and almost never vocabulary, and it is the part this class has met once, in 4.7.** **Item 1 is a sentential relative after a comma and _that_ is not available there.** **Item 4 is _No sooner … than_, and the _than_ further along the sentence is the trigger** — **a candidate who reads to the end of the sentence cannot miss it.** **Item 5 is _were it not for_, the inverted conditional**: _was_ is not available and _had_ would need _been_. **Item 6 is _what the better version would be_, where the verb is stranded at the end of the clause** — ⚠ **the commonest wrong answer here is _look_, from candidates who have supplied a meaning instead of reading the structure.** **Item 7 is a comparative _than_ twelve words after its _worse_**, and item 8 is _in so far as_, a fixed phrase worth learning whole. **Teach the habit the text itself describes: read to the end of the sentence before deciding what the gap needs.**'));
